{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/949558-bardo-travel","id":949558,"title":"Bardo Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-12T15:10:53-07:00","id":949558,"title":"Bardo Travel","content":"So, Bardos are the part of Mage I'm currently working on, and I had some ideas: one is that Bardos can be entered from either the physical world or the Astral, since Bardos are places where the power of Mania has managed to essentially turn nonexistence into reality. Entering a Bardo requires you to reach its Correspondence Zone on either side. So, the Bardo of Mars' CZ would be either Mars itself or parts of the Astral corresponding to other planets, science fiction, and so on. It's impossible to teleport straight into a Bardo- at most, you can use a Transportation+Space or Transportation+Mind working to travel to either of its Correspondence Zones. <br /> <br /> Bardos can be entered by spending a point of Mania anywhere in their Correspondence Zone. Beings without Mania can do this by spending stored Mania or using a Gatehouse. A Gatehouse is a Sanctum which has been built on the border between a Bardo and its Correspondence Zone, which provides a stable passage in and out. A Gatehouse can only be constructed if the Mage constructing it has a Paradigm that resonates with the Bardo. Some Mages collect tolls from their Gatehouses, while other Gatehouses have become Orphans and operate automatically.<br /> <br /> Bardos cannot connect to the Hedge, but can be entered through the Shadow of their Correspondence Zone. Bardos have no Shadow, however, and nothing can enter Twilight inside one. The Mania in the atmosphere forces everything inside them into fully manifested reality. Both the God-Machine and the Abyss are capable of claiming Bardos, but reports vary over whether or not either can actually create them. <br /> <br /> Prometheans and Bardos interact in the same way they interact with Sanctums: they do not cause Disquiet or Wastelands if the Bardo's Paradigm resonates with theirs. So an Ulgan would cause Disquiet and Paradox in a retro-futuristic city, while an Unfleshed would not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 08-12-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}